  "prompt_text": "The figure is a schematic of ion transport and interfacial structure in an electrolyte between a cathode on the left and an anode on the right. It emphasizes the electrical double layers near both electrodes, marked by the inner and outer Helmholtz planes (IHP and OHP). Near the negatively charged cathode, lithium ions accumulate close to the surface, while anions are positioned farther out; near the positively charged anode, the opposite arrangement appears, with anions concentrated near the surface and lithium ions farther away. Solvent molecules are shown surrounding the ions, especially in the interfacial regions.\n\nIn the bulk electrolyte between the electrodes, both Li+ and anions are dispersed and move in opposite directions along diffusion paths: lithium ions migrate toward the cathode, while anions migrate toward the anode. The diagram therefore illustrates how electrode charge redistributes ions and solvent at the interface and how this interfacial layering connects to ion diffusion through the electrolyte. Overall, the main message is the coexistence of bulk ion transport and structured charge separation at electrode surfaces in lithium battery electrolytes.",
